At one o'clock we all go to a restaurant nearby together.
The weather is beautiful today, so we sit outside.
We take a break and do not talk about the new project.
Katrin asks me about my time in Mexico.
"How long did you work there, Maya?" she asks.
"I worked in Mexico City for eight years," I answer.
"I have been a software engineer for eight years."
Sven eats his salad and looks at me.
"And what did you study?" he asks me.
"I studied computer science," I say.
Nele drinks her water and nods.
"I studied art in Berlin," says Nele.
We talk about our professions and laugh a lot.
Katrin smiles and pays the bill.
"We are a really good team," she says.
I agree with her and look forward to the work.
